     "<div>Dear GGIR list,<br></div><div><br></div><div>Just in case you missed it: Last week GGIR 2.4-0 was released.<br></div><div><br></div><div>The main addition is the incorporation of 28 metrics of daytime behavioural fragmentation. See vignette sections <a href=\"https://bit.ly/3wUy8Bg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://bit.ly/3wUy8Bg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792490480233000&amp;usg=AOvVaw07SvsLM06j8P8g59IwjQg9\">https://bit.ly/3wUy8Bg</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://bit.ly/3vVrMBD\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://bit.ly/3vVrMBD&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792490480233000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Mg6mPM9wtvIdKwnUYGuyX\">https://bit.ly/3vVrMBD</a>.\r\n<br></div><div>I am aware that documentation narrative could be improved, but this is at least an accurate minimalistic description.</div><div><br></div><div>Big thanks to Mathilde Chen, Manasa Yerramalla, and Séverine Sabia from <a href=\"https://cress-umr1153.fr/index.php/epiageing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cress-umr1153.fr/index.php/epiageing/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792490480233000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1IU_EKBH8DbgbbMlneOLGU\">https://cress-umr1153.fr/index.php/epiageing/</a> for all your support, brainstorming, and testing for this new functionality!<br></div><div><br></div><div>Best wishes,<br></div><div>Vincent</div><div><br></div><div>Dr. Vincent van Hees<br></div><div>Independent consultant<br></div><div><div><div><a title=\"https://accelting.com/\" href=\"https://accelting.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://accelting.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792490480233000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nLBQFnhNSYwCscxNdYc6N\">https://accelting.com/</a><br></div><div><div><br></div></div><div><div><a href=\"https://accelting.com/\" title